course: dictionary
lesson: 3093
title: Effective: what works well
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Effective is an adjective. Something effective works well and gives the result you want. To check, ask what it did and whether it got the result. «Many zoos fund rangers and scientists in places like Kenya, because protecting animals where they live is often more effective than breeding them in zoos.» The sentence compares two ways of helping animals and says one gets better results.
explain: Look at the clues. The word more before effective means the sentence is comparing two things. Protecting animals where they live gets better results for animals, so effective means it works well, and more effective means it works better than the other choice.
explain: Effective can also be used in formal notices. «The new rule is effective immediately» means it starts to apply from now. Here effective means in force, not good at a job. The words around it tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Effective is an adjective: effective, more effective, most effective.
fact: «Effective» means works well and gives the result you want.
fact: «Effective immediately» means it starts now, as in a formal notice.
fact: Useful phrases: «highly effective» means very good at working, «cost-effective» means good value for the money, and «take effect» means start to work.
fact: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence: «protecting animals is often more effective» can become «protecting animals often works better», and it still makes sense.
exercise: «Protecting animals where they live is often more effective than breeding them in zoos.» Which way gets better results for animals? | *Protecting animals where they live | Neither works at all | Breeding them in zoos | Both work exactly the same
exercise: Ms Patel says, «Our new soap is highly effective.» What does effective mean? | It is very expensive | It was made in a factory | *It works well and gets the result you want | It starts tomorrow
exercise: A notice says, «The new rule is effective immediately.» When does the rule start? | Next year | *From now | Never | Next week
test: Pupils test which method is most effective, such as which soap cleans best. What does most effective mean here? | Costs the least money | Has the longest name | *Cleans the most dirt, so it works best | Is the newest one
test: Which phrase means start to work or come into force? | take a photo | *take effect | take a break | take a bus
exam: Which word means works well and gets the result you want? | *effective | famished | luminous | glum
